.TH SNIP 1 "2026-10-21" "SnipCLI 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
snip \- fast, modern command-line snippet manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B snip
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B snip
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fICOMMAND_OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B SnipCLI
is a lightweight, zero-dependency command-line code snippet manager built in modern C++17.
It organizes code snippets with metadata, tags, and languages, persisting them to an atomic,
file-locked JSON repository.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR add " [\fIOPTIONS\fR]"
Store a new code snippet. Requires \fB\-\-title\fR, \fB\-\-lang\fR (or \fB\-\-language\fR),
and \fB\-\-code\fR.
.TP
.BR list " [\fIOPTIONS\fR]"
List all stored snippets in the repository.
.TP
.BR get " [\fIOPTIONS\fR]"
Retrieve and display a snippet by exact numeric identifier (\fB\-\-id\fR) or exact title (\fB\-\-title\fR).
Use \fB\-\-code\-only\fR to extract only the raw snippet contents.
.TP
.BR delete " [\fIOPTIONS\fR]"
Delete a snippet from the repository by ID (\fB\-\-id\fR) or title (\fB\-\-title\fR).
.TP
.BR search " [\fIOPTIONS\fR]"
Search stored snippets by tag (\fB\-\-tag\fR), title substring (\fB\-\-query\fR), or language (\fB\-\-language\fR).
.TP
.BR stats " [\fIOPTIONS\fR]"
Display aggregate repository statistics, including total snippet counts, language distributions, and tag usage.
.TP
.BR help " [\fICOMMAND\fR]"
Display usage documentation.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Global Options
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the command-line help summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the program version and architecture banner.
.SS Command Options
.TP
.BI \-\-title= TITLE
Specify the snippet title.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang= LANG ", " \-\-language= LANG
Specify the programming language of the snippet (e.g., \fBcpp\fR, \fBpython\fR, \fBrust\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-code= CODE
Specify the source code contents directly as a string argument.
.TP
.BI \-\-tags= TAGS
Specify a comma-separated list of tags (e.g., \fBgraph,dfs,tree\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-desc= DESC ", " \-\-description= DESC
Provide an optional descriptive text for the snippet.
.TP
.BI \-\-id= ID
Specify the unique positive integer ID of the snippet.
.TP
.B \-\-code\-only
Used with \fBget\fR. Outputs the raw snippet source code byte-for-byte to standard output without headers or syntax wrappers.
.TP
.BI \-\-format= FORMAT
Specify rendering view: \fBterminal\fR (default ANSI color formatting) or \fBmarkdown\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-query= QUERY
Used with \fBsearch\fR to filter snippets by case-insensitive title substring.
.TP
.BI \-\-tag= TAG
Used with \fBsearch\fR to filter snippets containing the specified tag.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SNIPCLI_STORAGE_PATH
Overrides the default storage path. Defaults to \fI~/.snipcli/snippets.json\fR.
.TP
.B SNIPCLI_LOCK_TIMEOUT_MS
Configures storage lock acquisition timeout in milliseconds (bounds: 1 to 600000 ms; default: 10000 ms).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to any non-empty value, disables ANSI color styling on terminal output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.snipcli/snippets.json
Default JSON file storage containing all saved snippets and metadata.
.TP
.I ~/.snipcli/snippets.json.lock
Advisory file lock used across concurrent instances to prevent race conditions during updates.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure (validation error, snippet not found, lock timeout, or filesystem storage error).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Add a new C++ snippet:
.RS
.B snip add \-\-title "Binary Exponentiation" \-\-lang cpp \-\-code "long long power(long long b, long long e) { ... }" \-\-tags math,algo
.RE
.PP
List all snippets in Markdown format:
.RS
.B snip list \-\-format markdown
.RE
.PP
Retrieve snippet #1 code directly into clipboard (X11):
.RS
.B snip get \-\-id 1 \-\-code\-only | xclip \-selection clipboard
.RE
.PP
Search for snippets with the tag "math":
.RS
.B snip search \-\-tag math
.RE
